From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: input: touchscreen: add Novatek NT36532

Add the touchscreen controller of the Novatek NT36532 touch and display
driver IC (TDDI). It sits on SPI, also reports an active stylus, and has
no flash: the host loads its firmware after every reset.

The firmware is tuned for the panel the IC drives. Boards that ship with
more than one panel list one firmware per panel in firmware-name and the
GPIOs that read the panel ID straps, whose value selects the entry. The
Lenovo Xiaoxin Pad Pro 12.7 (2025) reads one strap that tells its BOE
panel from its Tianma panels.

This is a binding of its own rather than another compatible in
novatek,nvt-ts.yaml, which describes I2C controllers that run from their
own flash: this one takes the SPI peripheral properties, a firmware per
panel and the stylus. The compatible names no bus, as asked in the review
of an earlier NT36xxx SPI binding, and keeps the -ts suffix of the
existing Novatek touchscreen compatibles, since the display side of the
IC is a separate device.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/c10b0b99-5bf2-47d3-b879-872f80e6883d@kernel.org

---
 .../input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml | 100 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 100 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e1625d2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/input/touchscreen/novatek,nt36532-ts.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Novatek NT36532 touchscreen controller
+
+maintainers:
+  - buntOS contributors <buntos@localhost>
+
+description: |
+  The touchscreen controller of the Novatek NT36532 touch and display driver
+  IC (TDDI), on an SPI bus. It also reports an active stylus.
+
+  The controller has no flash, so the host loads its firmware after every
+  reset. The firmware is tuned for the panel the IC drives. Boards that ship
+  with more than one panel list one firmware per panel and the GPIOs that
+  read the panel ID straps.
+
+  The stylus shares the coordinates of the touchscreen. touchscreen-x-mm and
+  touchscreen-y-mm give the length of the controller's X and Y axes, from
+  which the stylus resolution follows.
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: touchscreen.yaml#
+  - $ref: /schemas/spi/spi-peripheral-props.yaml#
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: novatek,nt36532-ts
+
+  reg:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  reset-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Touch controller reset (TP_RESX)
+
+  vcc-supply:
+    description: Analog supply
+
+  iovcc-supply:
+    description: Digital I/O supply
+
+  firmware-name:
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 4
+    description:
+      Firmware files, one per panel. The value read from
+      novatek,panel-id-gpios selects the entry; without those GPIOs the
+      first entry is used.
+
+  novatek,panel-id-gpios:
+    minItems: 1
+    maxItems: 2
+    description:
+      GPIOs that read the panel ID straps. The first GPIO gives bit 0 of the
+      index into firmware-name.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - interrupts
+  - reset-gpios
+  - firmware-name
+  - touchscreen-size-x
+  - touchscreen-size-y
+
+unevaluatedProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    #include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+
+    spi {
+        #address-cells = <1>;
+        #size-cells = <0>;
+
+        touchscreen@0 {
+            compatible = "novatek,nt36532-ts";
+            reg = <0>;
+            spi-max-frequency = <9600000>;
+            interrupts-extended = <&pio 9 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+            reset-gpios = <&pio 60 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+            iovcc-supply = <&vddio_1v8>;
+            firmware-name = "lenovo/tb375fc/novatek_ts_fw_boe.bin",
+                            "lenovo/tb375fc/novatek_ts_fw_tm.bin";
+            novatek,panel-id-gpios = <&pio 184 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+            touchscreen-size-x = <18401>;
+            touchscreen-size-y = <29441>;
+            touchscreen-x-mm = <171>;
+            touchscreen-y-mm = <273>;
+            touchscreen-swapped-x-y;
+        };
+    };
